<ul>
    <li>% Preset: the position taking taken by the upper agent. This percentage is also
        the maximum position taking that its downline agents can take. For example, if %
        Preset is X%, then position taking taken on all members of its line must be &#60;&#61;
        X.</li>
    <li>% Max Downline: the maximum position taking given to an agent. It is set by direct
        upline agent.</li>
    <li>% Min Downline: the minimum position taking which an agent and his downline agents
        must cover. It is set by direct upline agent.</li>
    <li>[x - y]: input range.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    <span class="note">Note:</span> only allow two numbers after the decimal point.
    For instance, 10.25 is a valid input, but 10.555 is not.
</p>